  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving lives and building resilience through humanitarian assistance and peacebuilding in ColombiaSaving lives and building resilience through humanitarian assistance and peacebuilding in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia continues to be the largest host of Venezuelan refugees and migrants with officially over 2.8 million. According to the results of the Joint Needs Assessment (JNA) led by the Interagency Group on Mixed Migration Flows - GIFMM, the principal needs for those who are in-destination are: food, employment, and household; to transit refugees and migrants (which are the most vulnerable group) their main needs are food, employment, and transport; and finally, to pendular population their main needs are food, employment, and health services. This project aims to support vulnerable populations affected by migration flows and armed conflict in the regions of Norte de Santander and Antioquia. It focuses on providing temporary shelter solutions, cash-for-rent assistance, and essential health and protection services to migrants, refugees, returnees, internally displaced persons (IDPs), and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
